      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Cypriot president Nikos Christodoulides and Northern Cypriot president Tufan Erhürman agreed to establish two additional crossings across the United Nations Buffer Zone in Cyprus and to hold further peace negotiations.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-09:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 9 November 2026, the two leaders met in a UN buffer zone and agreed to open two new border crossings and to resume talks before the end of 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384776266:479"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The dispute between the Greek and Turkish communities in Cyprus over how the island should be governed is ongoing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384776266:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The map shows Cyprus, the island where the reports place this story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-09:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The Cyprus problem began on 1 April 1955 and ended on 18 August 1974.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q245831:P580",
        "wd:Q245831:P582"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "The report was carried by Reuters.",
